Role: Senior Gameplay Programmer & Debugger Task: Fix "Invisible Projectile" Bug via Logic Enforcement & Debug Rendering Context: The user confirmed "Option B": No projectiles are spawning at all. This means combat.ts is skipping spawnProjectile() because the skills likely have projectileSpeed: 0 or undefined in the database, causing them to execute instantly as invisible hits.

Objective:

Logic Injection (combat.ts): Intercept skills with projectile-like visuals (ARROW, FIREBALL) and FORCE them to have a speed, ensuring they enter the projectile logic path.

Render Safety (renderer.ts): Prevent math crashes (NaN) and draw a Magenta Box if the sprite is missing, so we can see the logic is working even if assets fail.

Required Changes:

1. engine/systems/combat.ts - Force Projectile Spawning
Modify the Cast Completion block in updateAgentCasting.

Logic: Before checking s.projectileSpeed, check s.visual.

Rule: If s.visual is ARROW, FIREBALL, or BOLT (projectile types), AND s.projectileSpeed is missing or <= 0:

Override: Set s.projectileSpeed = 600 (or a reasonable default).

This forces the code to enter the this.spawnProjectile(...) block instead of executeInstantSkill.

2. engine/renderer.ts - Render Safety & Debugging
Modify collectRenderables (Projectile Loop):

Fix NaN Crash: When calculating dir, check if p.targetPos and p.x, p.y are nearly identical (distance < 1). If so, use a fallback vector {x: 1, y: 0} or the last known velocity to avoid Vector.normalize(0,0).

Pink Box Fallback: In the draw callback:

TypeScript

const img = AssetManager.getProjectile(...);
if (img) {
    ctx.drawImage(img, ...);
} else {
    // DEBUG: Draw Magenta Box if asset is missing
    ctx.fillStyle = '#ff00ff';
    ctx.fillRect(-10, -10, 20, 20);
}
Action: Please provide the refactored code blocks for combat.ts (updateAgentCasting) and renderer.ts (collectRenderables) incorporating these fixes.

